 money for rh1) | 186666666666667 → 20000000000000 wei | $1.40 |\n| 3 | q_6 | eth-bridge-wbtc-robinhood | 247500 → 246666 WBTC | $1.4004 |\n| 4 | q_9 | rh-swap-wbtc-eth (rh1) | 246666 WBTC → 49233200000000000 wei ETH | $0.36 |\n| 5 | q_5 | eth-bridge-eth-arbitrum (gas money for arb1) | 206666666666667 → 40000000000000 wei | $1.40 |\n| 6 | q_7 | eth-bridge-wbtc-arbitrum | 247500 → 246666 WBTC | $1.4004 |\n| 7 | q_10 | arb-swap-wbtc-usdc (arb1) | 246666 WBTC → 147699600 USDC | $0.36 |\n\n**Why legs 2 and 5 are there:** your Robinhood (rh1) and Arbitrum (arb1) wallets have no ETH to pay gas for their swaps. arb1 also has to keep enough ETH for one more transaction afterwards, because it will be holding USDC.\n- Each bridge takes a fixed fee of about 166666666666667 wei (about $0.50), so smaller top-ups don't work. I tried 20000000000000 and 40000000000000 wei and both failed with `amount_too_small`.\n- The amounts above are sized so exactly what's needed arrives.\n\n**Expected balances at the end**\n- **eth1 (Ethereum):** 48106666666666666 wei ETH, 0 WBTC, 0 USDC. This assumes each transaction costs exactly the listed gas amount.\n- **rh1 (Robinhood):** 49233200000000000 wei ETH.\n- **arb1 (Arbitrum):** 20000000000000 wei ETH, which is exactly one transaction's gas, plus 147699600 USDC.\n\n**Cheaper than the alternative:** swapping to USDC on Ethereum and then bridging the USDC to Arbitrum would cost $13.7604 and deliver 145000000 USDC instead of 147699600.\n\n**Two things that could change during execution**\n- **The 50/50 split:** the halves (247500 each) are based on the quoted 495000 WBTC. If the first swap fills differently, I'll split the actual balance and get new prices for the later legs.\n- **Price expiry:** prices expire after 300s, and the route takes about 285s because there are four 60s bridges. The last legs may need fresh prices for the same amounts."}]},{"role":"user","sequence":26,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes, go ahead with that plan."}]},{"r